{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"84594709c13346e5ec686080b03588b3f979449a8ba523683005f8176bb831cc","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_ref_lock.py unit test","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py","test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote","_git()","git --git-dir","git -C","GIT_CONFIG_COUNT","GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0","safe.bareRepository=explicit","cat-file","rev-parse","tests/_git_upkeep.py","test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["git bare repository","safe.bareRepository explicit policy","test portability","implicit discovery","git -C refusal"],"propositions":["test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote fails with exit 128 when the host injects git's safe.bareRepository=explicit security policy via environment","Under safe.bareRepository=explicit, git refuses implicit discovery of bare repositories via 'git -C <bare.git>' but permits explicit naming via 'git --git-dir'","The test's _git() helper uses 'git -C' against bare fixtures for cat-file and rev-parse operations, violating the bare-repo portability contract that other tests enforce","Production _ref_lock code never executes 'git -C' inside a bare repository, so this is a test-only defect","The fix replaces bare-repository git invocations with a --git-dir helper matching prior art in _git_upkeep.py and test_concurrency_regression.py"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787543541929657001,"uuid":"b61a7d15-9904-4ae3-a585-61a483737fed"}